From cfac6707cb82caaf9b4d0cdbe7aa46f6fb20ac1f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 01:27:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] l5-pmus-live: owner-listed venue-superset cost correction,
 off by default

The diagnostic of 2026-11-20 found 40 settled markets inside the account-wide
loss figure where the venue's fills contain more than this ledger recorded
(one leg adopted, the other never seen) and the row is booked at $1 a share.

attest_retired_market_cost gains one more form, VENUE_SUPERSET_OWNER_LISTED,
reachable only when the caller hands in the owner's listed figures for that
market and every one equals what is found: both venue quantities and costs,
both ledger quantities, settlement value, booked and corrected result. It
also requires the ledger quantity contained in the venue's, every held side
never costed, zero readable fees, a feed read to its end, and a settlement
after the last accounting re-anchor. Without a listing the method behaves
exactly as before.

l5_venue_superset_correction is the only caller. OFF unless
L5_VENUE_SUPERSET_CORRECTION is set. INSPECT runs the real correction on a
copy of the ledger that cannot be saved. APPLY writes only when
L5_VENUE_SUPERSET_CORRECTION_APPROVED equals the SHA-256 of the shipped
manifest (40 markets, +97.3165 in total). Two unreadable rows are excluded.
No limit is changed.

45 tests. One existing allowlist changed: the image data-file guard now
names the manifest, as it does the earlier cost-basis manifests.

Not deployed, not applied.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01HTk927uH8zwpj6gLES92PF
